GPL-2.0-or-later and is not covered by the CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 terms above.

Every generated mesh under `public/models/` (`*.glb`; `ASSETS.md` names the
Oolite `.dat` model or models each file is converted from) is converted with
Wegolite's own code from the Oolite `.dat` models, and each is a derivative work
of those models: it remains CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, with attribution to the
Oolite contributors, non-commercial use only, and share-alike terms. The
conversion is a format change (glTF binary), an axis convention change and a
material projection — no authorship of the geometry is claimed.

The baked greyscale emissive maps under `public/textures/*_emissive.png` are
derived from Oolite's PNG textures by Wegolite's build, which reads the source
alpha channel and writes a new greyscale image; they are derivative works of
those textures and remain CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, under the same
attribution, non-commercial and share-alike terms. The ship, station and navigation buoy
textures under `public/textures/*.webp` are the same Oolite PNG textures
re-encoded to WebP by Wegolite's build (lossy for the diffuse and specular
maps, near-lossless for the normal maps, with the unused alpha channel of the
diffuse and normal maps dropped); they are derivative works of those textures
and remain CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, under the same attribution,
non-commercial and share-alike terms. The four sky textures
`public/textures/oolite-nebula-*.png` are byte-identical to the vendored
originals and are redistributed unmodified under the same licence. The two
explosion particle textures `public/textures/oolite-particle-cloud2.png` and
`public/textures/oolite-particle-flash.png` are likewise byte-identical copies
of the vendored originals, redistributed unmodified under the same licence. The
unmodified source PNGs are kept under `third_party/oolite/Textures/`.

The generated dock-port record `src/content/generated/dock-port.json` is
measured at build time from the vendored Oolite `.dat` models (`oolite_coriolis`,
`oolite_coriolis_tris`, `oolite_coriolis_faceplate`, `oolite_coriolis_dock` and
`oolite_cobra3`). It is a derivative work of those models and remains
CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, with attribution to the Oolite contributors,
non-commercial use only and share-alike terms.

The generated NPC ship record file `src/content/generated/ships-npc.json` is
compiled at build time from the vendored Oolite `shipdata.plist` (with
`like_ship` resolved, for nine NPC ships: the roles, AI name, scan class, model
and display name, the maximum energy and energy recharge rate, the forward, aft,
port and starboard weapon types and positions gated by `weapon_facings`, the
flight constants (maximum speed, roll and pitch rate, and thrust),
`likely_cargo`, `max_cargo`, `fragment_chance` and `explosion_type`) and from
the vendored Oolite `.dat` models: the `mass` of each record is computed by
Wegolite's port of Oolite's octree volume rule over the hull and its solid
subentities, and the `radius` of each record is computed from the same vendored
`.dat` hull model (the distance of its farthest vertex from the model origin, as
Oolite computes its collision radius), and the `boundingBox` of each record is
the bounding box of each hull (the extremes of its vendored `.dat` vertices). It
is a derivative work of `shipdata.plist` and of those models and remains
CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, with attribution to the Oolite contributors,
non-commercial use only and share-alike terms.

The generated hull file `src/content/generated/ships-hulls.json` is compiled at
build time from the vendored Oolite `.dat` models of the player Cobra Mk III
(`oolite_cobra3`) and the nine NPC ships: for each hull it carries the octree
Wegolite's port of Oolite's octree builder computes from the model, and the hull
collision radius computed as for `ships-npc.json`. It is a derivative work of
those models and remains CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, with attribution to the
Oolite contributors, non-commercial use only and share-alike terms.

The generated static hull file `src/content/generated/ships-static-hulls.json`
is compiled at build time from the vendored Oolite `.dat` models and the
vendored `shipdata.plist` (with `like_ship` resolved): for the Coriolis station,
the navigation buoy, the cargo barrel and the alloy plate it carries the octree
Wegolite's port of Oolite's octree builder computes from each model, the
collision radius computed as for `ships-client.json` and `ships-debris.json`,
the `frangible` flag, and each solid subentity's octree, authored position and
mass computed from its model; it also carries the display names of the station,
the two buoys, the barrel and the plate. It is a derivative work of
`shipdata.plist` and of those models and remains CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL,
with attribution to the Oolite contributors, non-commercial use only and
share-alike terms. Nothing is vendored or changed for it, so
`third_party/oolite/CHECKSUMS.sha256` is untouched.

The generated debris catalogue `src/content/generated/ships-debris.json` is
compiled at build time from the vendored Oolite `shipdata.plist` debris entries
(with `like_ship` resolved: the cargo barrel, the alloy plate and the wreckage
entries; for each, its role, model and tumble rates `max_flight_roll` and
`max_flight_pitch`) and from the vendored Oolite `.dat` models: the `mass` and
`radius` of each record are computed from its model as for `ships-npc.json`. It
is a derivative work of `shipdata.plist` and of those models and remains
CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, with attribution to the Oolite contributors,
non-commercial use only and share-alike terms.

The generated explosion settings `src/content/generated/explosions.json` are
compiled at build time from the vendored Oolite `explosions.plist` (the default
ship explosion entry: its alpha, colour order, particle count, duration, growth
rate, size and texture, with Oolite's defaults for the keys it omits). They are
a derivative work of `explosions.plist` and remain CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL,
with attribution to the Oolite contributors, non-commercial use only and
share-alike terms.

The `mass` values in `src/content/generated/ships-client.json` (the player Cobra
Mk III, the Coriolis station and the navigation buoy) are computed the same way
from the vendored Oolite `oolite_cobra3` model, the four Coriolis models
(`oolite_coriolis`, `oolite_coriolis_tris`, `oolite_coriolis_faceplate` and
`oolite_coriolis_dock`) and the two buoy models (`oolite_buoy` and
`oolite_buoy_subents`). That file is a derivative work of `shipdata.plist` and
of those models and remains CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, never GPL, with attribution to the
Oolite contributors, non-commercial use only and share-alike terms.

